Marks the author places on their own words — emphasis and the small typographic and semantic marks.

<section #ag-abbr | `<abbr>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<abbr>`.

<code #code:ag-abbr-1>
The <abbr title="Document Object Model" | DOM> is the browser API for HTML.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-abbr-1>
The <abbr title="Document Object Model" | DOM> is the browser API for HTML.
</minipage>

*Standard pattern — abbreviation with its expansion as the title
kwarg. Browsers show the expansion in a hover tooltip.*

</section>

<section #ag-b | `<b>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<b>`; markdown `**…**`.

<code #code:ag-b-1>
The keyword <b type=keyword | recursion> is fundamental.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-b-1>
The keyword <b type=keyword | recursion> is fundamental.
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-em | `<em>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<em>`.

<code #code:ag-em-1>
This has *emphasized* content.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-em-1>
This has *emphasized* content.
</minipage>

*Plain markdown emphasis with single asterisks (or single underscores)
produces &lt;em&gt; elements. This is the most common authoring path.*

</section>

<section #ag-i | `<i>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<i>`; markdown `*…*` (or `_…_`).

<code #code:ag-i-1>
The species is <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana>.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-i-1>
The species is <i type=taxonomic | Loxodonta africana>.
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-kbd | `<kbd>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<kbd>`.

<code #code:ag-kbd-1>
Press <kbd | Ctrl+C> to copy.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-kbd-1>
Press <kbd | Ctrl+C> to copy.
</minipage>

*Single chord as a kbd block. Browsers render &lt;kbd&gt; in a
monospace font by default, distinguishing it from surrounding
prose.*

</section>

<section #ag-output | `<output>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<output>`.

<code #code:ag-output-1>
The function returns <output | 42> for the test input.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-output-1>
The function returns <output | 42> for the test input.
</minipage>

*Result of a calculation in prose. &lt;output&gt; is semantically
distinct from &lt;samp&gt; — &lt;samp&gt; is what a program prints (a
display artifact); &lt;output&gt; is the result of a computation
(a semantic value). Browsers render both similarly.*

</section>

<section #ag-s | `<s>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<s>`; markdown `~~…~~`.

<code #code:ag-s-1>
The price is ~~$50~~ now $40.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-s-1>
The price is ~~$50~~ now $40.
</minipage>

*GFM's tilde syntax produces &lt;s&gt; elements. The most common
authoring path for casual strikethrough.*

</section>

<section #ag-samp | `<samp>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<samp>`.

<code #code:ag-samp-1>
The command prints <samp | Hello, world!> to stdout.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-samp-1>
The command prints <samp | Hello, world!> to stdout.
</minipage>

*Sample output from a program. Browsers render &lt;samp&gt; in a
monospace font by default, distinguishing it from surrounding
prose.*

</section>

<section #ag-strong | `<strong>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<strong>`.

<code #code:ag-strong-1>
This is **strongly emphasized** content.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-strong-1>
This is **strongly emphasized** content.
</minipage>

*Plain markdown with double asterisks (or double underscores) produces
&lt;strong&gt; elements.*

</section>

<section #ag-sub | `<sub>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<sub>`.

<code #code:ag-sub-1>
Water is H<sub | 2>O.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-sub-1>
Water is H<sub | 2>O.
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-sup | `<sup>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<sup>`.

<code #code:ag-sup-1>
The 1<sup | st> edition of the work.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-sup-1>
The 1<sup | st> edition of the work.
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-term | `<term>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<term>`.

<code #code:ag-term-1>
An <term | eigenvector> is a non-zero vector that scales under a linear transformation.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-term-1>
An <term | eigenvector> is a non-zero vector that scales under a linear transformation.
</minipage>

*Standard term introduction. The element marks the word as
"this is a term being introduced," typically rendered in italic
or bold by default CSS.*

</section>

<section #ag-u | `<u>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<u>`.

<code #code:ag-u-1>
The author wrote <u type=misspelling | recieve> in the original.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-u-1>
The author wrote <u type=misspelling | recieve> in the original.
</minipage>

</section>

<section #ag-var | `<var>`>

Compiles to eHTML `<var>`.

<code #code:ag-var-1>
The function takes a parameter <var | n> and returns <var | n>²+1.
</code>

<minipage #mp:ag-var-1>
The function takes a parameter <var | n> and returns <var | n>²+1.
</minipage>

*Variable names in prose. Browsers render &lt;var&gt; in italic by
default, distinguishing it from surrounding prose.*

</section>
